WEBVTT

00:00:00.242 --> 00:00:02.535
- Previously on The O.C.:
- You and Marissa want different things.

00:00:02.744 --> 00:00:05.412
- You don't know what she wants!
- I know what she doesn't want.

00:00:05.621 --> 00:00:07.622
I wanna live with Dad.
At least for now.

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:09.873
Then train me
in the ways of women.

00:00:10.082 --> 00:00:13.292
- Why are you helping him with Summer?
- Seth doesn't see me that way.

00:00:13.501 --> 00:00:15.043
And you're gonna let that slide?

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:17.128
Is this all part of the plan?

00:00:17.336 --> 00:00:19.755
This is a policy-changing,
career-making piece of litigation.

00:00:19.963 --> 00:00:22.131
- My wife's company is the plaintiff.
- Her father's company.

00:00:22.339 --> 00:00:23.882
- You're gonna take this.
- It's who you married.

00:00:24.091 --> 00:00:27.051
If your marriage can't survive this,
what kind of marriage is it?

00:00:27.259 --> 00:00:29.260
I wanna make it work. No matter what.

00:00:48.606 --> 00:00:50.691
- Ticklish.
- Sorry.

00:01:02.239 --> 00:01:05.783
- What time do you have?
- Almost 11.

00:01:05.992 --> 00:01:09.077
What time do you have
to be back at your dad's?

00:01:09.285 --> 00:01:11.870
- Soon.
- How soon?

00:01:12.079 --> 00:01:14.080
Now.

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:25.712
You can't call? Say you'll be late?

00:01:27.088 --> 00:01:28.964
I'm already late.

00:01:29.173 --> 00:01:31.258
It's a school night.

00:01:35.177 --> 00:01:38.095
It's too bad you don't still live next door.

00:01:38.304 --> 00:01:41.055
Yeah. But then I'd have
to talk to my mom.

00:01:41.264 --> 00:01:43.932
You haven't talked to her?

00:01:44.141 --> 00:01:45.683
No.

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:48.685
She keeps trying to call me,
but there's no way I'm...

00:01:48.852 --> 00:01:50.103
Hey.

00:01:52.229 --> 00:01:53.605
Sorry.

00:01:59.358 --> 00:02:04.195
Maybe this weekend,
we could spend a whole night together.

00:02:07.697 --> 00:02:11.199
You know, we could go out,
do something.

00:02:11.408 --> 00:02:13.659
Finally have our first official date.

00:02:14.743 --> 00:02:17.787
No school. No parents. Just us.

00:02:19.413 --> 00:02:21.497
Saturday night.

00:02:22.373 --> 00:02:23.624
Cool.

00:02:30.253 --> 00:02:34.589
Hey, Ryan. Sandy's stuck at the...
Oh, my God! I'm so sorry.

00:02:34.797 --> 00:02:37.549
Hey, Kirsten.

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:42.052
Hey, Marissa.
I didn't know that you had company.

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:46.138
Yeah. Well, I was just gonna go.
So see you.

00:02:46.346 --> 00:02:48.431
- Later.
- Good night.

00:02:48.639 --> 00:02:50.766
Drive safely.

00:02:53.017 --> 00:02:54.476
It's never happened with Seth.

00:03:26.121 --> 00:03:29.665
- You walked in on them?
- Well, at least I knocked.

00:03:29.873 --> 00:03:32.875
Ryan and Marissa Cooper.
I knew it. Didn't I tell you?

00:03:33.042 --> 00:03:35.002
- No.
- No?

00:03:36.711 --> 00:03:40.297
Sandy, maybe you should talk to him.

00:03:41.506 --> 00:03:44.341
- About what?
- You know. Sex.

00:03:44.549 --> 00:03:48.135
- Sounds like he knows what he's doing.
- I mean, sex in the house.

00:03:48.343 --> 00:03:51.095
- We obviously don't believe in that.
- We don't?

00:03:51.262 --> 00:03:54.972
Based on my recent experience,
or lack thereof, I'd have to say no.

00:03:55.181 --> 00:03:58.433
Hey, I'm not the one coming home
from the office at midnight.

00:03:58.641 --> 00:04:00.267
You come home at 11:45.

00:04:00.476 --> 00:04:05.896
I might be coming home earlier
if your firm wasn't suing my company.

00:04:07.147 --> 00:04:11.399
Well, look, maybe we'll get lucky
and settle at the conference tomorrow.

00:04:11.566 --> 00:04:14.401
Maybe we'll get lucky tonight.

00:04:14.568 --> 00:04:17.028
I'd settle for that. What time?

00:04:17.236 --> 00:04:19.404
- How about 8?
- Eight?

00:04:19.613 --> 00:04:21.822
- Nine?
- Nine-thirty?

00:04:22.031 --> 00:04:25.158
- Lf you're not home by 10:00...
- Yeah?

00:04:25.366 --> 00:04:27.951
...I'm gonna start without you.

00:04:32.204 --> 00:04:33.830
Morning!

00:04:35.456 --> 00:04:36.999
Hi.

00:04:37.207 --> 00:04:40.292
- We're all very proud.
- Thanks.

00:04:40.459 --> 00:04:45.212
And sorry. I just wanted
to say sorry about last night.

00:04:45.421 --> 00:04:48.256
- Sorry about what? What did I miss?
- You should talk to him.

00:04:48.422 --> 00:04:50.882
I appreciate you guys
being so cool about everything.

00:04:51.049 --> 00:04:53.551
- Cool about what?
- I'll see you tonight.

00:04:53.759 --> 00:04:55.594
We should get going too.

00:04:55.802 --> 00:04:58.220
Not till somebody tells me
what happened.

00:04:58.429 --> 00:05:00.889
Mom, would you please fill me in?

00:05:01.097 --> 00:05:04.391
Mom!
I get it, I'm just here for comic relief.

00:05:07.017 --> 00:05:10.853
So, what exactly did my mom
catch you guys doing?

00:05:11.062 --> 00:05:13.813
- Nothing.
- Nothing, huh?

00:05:14.022 --> 00:05:16.773
- So you guys haven't...?
- Haven't even had our first date.

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:20.067
- Last night doesn't count?
- No. We're going out Saturday night.

00:05:20.276 --> 00:05:22.110
Good. Great.

00:05:23.111 --> 00:05:26.446
But you have before, right?

00:05:26.655 --> 00:05:30.365
Okay. That's what I thought.
I didn't want to jump to conclusions.

00:05:30.574 --> 00:05:33.534
My experience is sort of limited.

00:05:33.742 --> 00:05:35.410
- And?
- And what?

00:05:35.619 --> 00:05:37.995
Was it awesome?

00:05:38.204 --> 00:05:41.164
Which time?

00:05:41.372 --> 00:05:43.290
There were...?
How many times were there?

00:05:43.499 --> 00:05:48.085
- Same girl or different girls?
- There were different girls?

00:05:49.210 --> 00:05:51.420
How many different girls were there?

00:05:55.548 --> 00:05:57.299
I have to sit down.

00:05:57.507 --> 00:06:01.135
- So, what happened? I want details.
- Nothing happened.

00:06:01.343 --> 00:06:04.303
- What's his problem?
- There is no problem.

00:06:04.512 --> 00:06:08.639
- I just don't know if I'm ready yet.
- But Luke took care of that painful part.

00:06:08.806 --> 00:06:11.474
Yeah, and look how well
that turned out.

00:06:11.683 --> 00:06:15.060
Look, Ryan and I, we're still
getting to know each other.

00:06:15.268 --> 00:06:18.937
- We're going on our first date Saturday.
- That should be romantic.

00:06:19.146 --> 00:06:22.231
Sorry, Coop. It's just, what does
Chino know about a date?

00:06:22.398 --> 00:06:24.941
Where he's from,
they don't even have a P.F. Chang's.

00:06:26.025 --> 00:06:30.153
When you lost your virginity,
I was playing Magic: The Gathering.

00:06:30.319 --> 00:06:33.780
- You still play Magic.
- Yeah, but not as much.

00:06:33.988 --> 00:06:36.824
- Hey. What are you guys talking about?
- Nothing.

00:06:37.032 --> 00:06:38.866
Ryan was telling me about
your big date.

00:06:39.075 --> 00:06:40.784
He's got a whole thing happening.

00:06:40.993 --> 00:06:43.077
Wow, there's a whole thing happening?

00:06:43.286 --> 00:06:47.038
Yeah, but it's a surprise. It's gonna
be the best date ever. I have to go.

00:06:47.455 --> 00:06:49.790
- Summer, I'll walk you to bio.
- I can walk myself.

00:06:49.998 --> 00:06:51.791
Great, then you can walk me too.

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:55.002
Best date ever, huh?

00:06:58.545 --> 00:07:01.047
The ecological risk assessment
backs up our claim...

00:07:01.255 --> 00:07:03.549
...that the land Caleb Nichol
plans to develop...

00:07:03.757 --> 00:07:07.009
...should be considered as wetlands.
- Oh, great.

00:07:07.218 --> 00:07:09.427
Great. We'll get into that tomorrow.

00:07:09.636 --> 00:07:11.929
What do you got tonight?
A hot date?

00:07:12.137 --> 00:07:13.388
Yeah.

00:07:14.639 --> 00:07:18.266
Sandy Cohen, you are cheating
on me, with your wife.

00:07:18.683 --> 00:07:19.934
I'm trying.

00:07:20.142 --> 00:07:22.644
- What is it, your anniversary?
- No.

00:07:22.852 --> 00:07:26.605
We haven't seen each other
in a while, so we thought we'd...

00:07:26.813 --> 00:07:29.815
Go on a date. Why not? Good idea.

00:07:29.982 --> 00:07:32.817
It's not like we have
our settlement conference tomorrow...

00:07:32.984 --> 00:07:36.527
...where the fate of Orange County's
environment hangs in the balance.

00:07:37.945 --> 00:07:43.073
All right. The date will even be better
after the conference. Less stress.

00:07:44.616 --> 00:07:47.951
Dad, good news...
I'm sorry, I didn't know you...

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:50.328
- Julie.
- Kirsten.

00:07:50.536 --> 00:07:53.413
Your father and I
were just talking about you.

00:07:53.622 --> 00:07:58.124
This man just single-handedly saved
the children's hospital benefit.

00:07:58.333 --> 00:08:01.085
- I did no such thing.
- He's so modest.

00:08:01.251 --> 00:08:05.212
I'd just lost the Buckley yacht,
when he agreed to let me use his.

00:08:05.421 --> 00:08:08.089
The man just gives and gives.

00:08:08.256 --> 00:08:12.050
I didn't know that you were organizing
the children's hospital benefit.

00:08:12.258 --> 00:08:16.761
I wasn't going to, but it's time I stopped
dwelling on my own problems...

00:08:16.969 --> 00:08:20.388
...and got back to focusing
on the needs of others, right?

00:08:20.597 --> 00:08:22.723
So must be off.

00:08:22.931 --> 00:08:24.641
Cal.

00:08:26.184 --> 00:08:28.226
I owe you bigtime.

00:08:28.435 --> 00:08:30.478
- Bye, Kirsten.
- Bye, Julie.

00:08:33.396 --> 00:08:36.398
- She is something, isn't she?
- She is that.

00:08:37.524 --> 00:08:39.859
You know, you are now
the official sponsor...

00:08:40.067 --> 00:08:42.736
...of the Julie Cooper Comeback Tour.

00:08:43.319 --> 00:08:44.570
It's for charity.

00:08:44.778 --> 00:08:47.614
After all the bad press
your husband's been getting us...

00:08:47.780 --> 00:08:50.032
...it can't hurt to be involved
in a good cause.

00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:51.616
So, what was your good news?

00:08:51.783 --> 00:08:54.701
We can have that
working dinner after all.

00:08:54.910 --> 00:08:58.829
- Sandy cancelled your date?
- They have some last-minute prep work.

00:08:59.037 --> 00:09:01.664
- By "they" you mean Sandy and...
- Rachel, yes.

00:09:01.831 --> 00:09:04.791
She's attractive?
And he got in at midnight last night?

00:09:04.999 --> 00:09:07.042
- I trust him.
- You know what they say.

00:09:07.251 --> 00:09:09.419
The only man a girl should trust
is her father.

00:09:09.627 --> 00:09:12.212
They're working together. That's all.

00:09:15.047 --> 00:09:18.341
I suggest we do the same.
See you later.

00:09:20.301 --> 00:09:23.052
Why don't you just take her
to dinner and a movie?

00:09:23.261 --> 00:09:24.512
It's a classic combination.

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:27.472
Because somebody promised her
the best date ever.

00:09:27.639 --> 00:09:31.266
I went ahead and did a little recon
on your behalf. I was extremely stealth.

00:09:31.474 --> 00:09:33.434
I spoke to Summer, okay?
And I asked her...

00:09:33.642 --> 00:09:36.769
...what Marissa would wanna do
on a date, what she'd really enjoy.

00:09:36.978 --> 00:09:39.062
- She told me she didn't know.
- How helpful.

00:09:39.271 --> 00:09:43.273
But Summer's three favorite activities
are shopping, tanning and waxing.

00:09:43.482 --> 00:09:45.692
Maybe there's something there.
Use that.

00:09:45.900 --> 00:09:49.361
And here I thought
Summer was superficial.

00:09:49.569 --> 00:09:53.280
I have no car, no money. Whatever
I do is just gonna disappoint her.

00:09:53.488 --> 00:09:56.490
- What do you usually do on dates?
- Never actually been on one.

00:09:56.657 --> 00:09:59.033
Wait, you just told me that...

00:09:59.242 --> 00:10:05.037
Yeah, I've hung out with girls,
but just never really went out.

00:10:06.538 --> 00:10:09.039
- Oh, got it.
- I'm gonna go to class.

00:10:09.248 --> 00:10:11.624
- I'll keep working on it.
- You've done enough.

00:10:11.833 --> 00:10:14.376
Bye. Come on.

00:10:15.627 --> 00:10:18.671
What do you think Summer's
three favorite movies are?

00:10:18.879 --> 00:10:22.548
Battleship Potemkin,
The Seventh Seal and Shoah.

00:10:22.756 --> 00:10:24.883
- Definitely.
- What?

00:10:25.091 --> 00:10:28.802
Can we not talk about Summer?
We talk about her all the time.

00:10:29.010 --> 00:10:30.803
No, we don't.

00:10:31.012 --> 00:10:34.514
We don't. We talk about
all sorts of things. Music, sailing.

00:10:34.722 --> 00:10:37.182
Right. About how you named
your boat after her...

00:10:37.391 --> 00:10:40.392
...how you made her a CD of songs
with the word "summer" in it.

00:10:40.601 --> 00:10:43.269
Sorry. I was under the impression
that we were friends...

00:10:43.478 --> 00:10:45.604
...who, I don't know,
talk about our thoughts.

00:10:45.812 --> 00:10:49.690
We are. So I guess you're
finally hearing some of mine.

00:10:52.525 --> 00:10:55.110
I'm gonna go back for dessert.

00:11:04.949 --> 00:11:07.910
Hey, Dad. I'm...

00:11:08.118 --> 00:11:09.661
...home.

00:11:09.827 --> 00:11:12.496
- Hi, sweetie.
- What are you doing here?

00:11:12.704 --> 00:11:16.498
Your mother was in the neighborhood
and wanted to see how we're doing.

00:11:16.707 --> 00:11:20.584
- How are we doing, Mom?
- Why don't you come here and talk to us.

00:11:20.793 --> 00:11:22.752
Come on over and sit down.

00:11:31.591 --> 00:11:33.426
I'm throwing a party.

00:11:33.634 --> 00:11:36.469
I'm hosting the children's hospital benefit
this Saturday.

00:11:36.636 --> 00:11:39.638
They're trying to build
a new wing for the children.

00:11:39.846 --> 00:11:43.807
I'd love it if you could both be there.
Your father's already agreed.

00:11:44.016 --> 00:11:45.850
No. No way.

00:11:46.058 --> 00:11:48.018
Marissa, honey...

00:11:48.226 --> 00:11:52.187
...this party is a chance for us to show
the community that we still belong...

00:11:52.396 --> 00:11:54.439
...that we're still a family.

00:11:54.647 --> 00:11:58.775
Yes, we've suffered some setbacks,
your father's business in particular.

00:11:58.983 --> 00:12:02.569
But it's important to let everybody know
the Cooper family is back.

00:12:02.777 --> 00:12:04.820
Why do you care
what other people think?

00:12:05.029 --> 00:12:09.865
Look, Marissa, no one has fewer nice
things to say about your mother than me.

00:12:10.073 --> 00:12:12.116
No offense.

00:12:12.325 --> 00:12:14.618
But she's been pouring
her heart out to me...

00:12:14.826 --> 00:12:19.621
...and I think you're gonna wanna hear
what she has to say.

00:12:20.455 --> 00:12:25.667
Marissa, I am so sorry for the way
I handled things at the hospital.

00:12:25.875 --> 00:12:27.793
I was scared.

00:12:28.001 --> 00:12:30.294
And I was wrong.

00:12:30.503 --> 00:12:32.879
Everything I cared about
was falling apart...

00:12:33.088 --> 00:12:36.382
...and I was blaming everybody
but myself.

00:12:39.509 --> 00:12:42.886
I just want us to feel
like a family again.

00:12:45.012 --> 00:12:50.057
I know it's gonna take some time,
and I'm gonna need your help.

00:12:51.016 --> 00:12:54.018
Will you help me?

00:13:03.565 --> 00:13:05.983
Wow, knocking. It's open!

00:13:12.154 --> 00:13:13.446
Bad news.

00:13:13.655 --> 00:13:18.283
I know you had Saturday night
all planned, but something's come up.

00:13:18.491 --> 00:13:19.950
Oh, that sucks.

00:13:20.159 --> 00:13:23.286
We're gonna be spending
a romantic night on a yacht...

00:13:23.494 --> 00:13:27.955
...for this charity event
hosted by my mom.

00:13:28.497 --> 00:13:29.790
Your mom hates me.

00:13:29.998 --> 00:13:32.458
No, she doesn't hate you.
She just doesn't know you.

00:13:32.667 --> 00:13:34.209
Now she'll have her chance.

00:13:34.376 --> 00:13:37.378
We had a date Saturday night.
There was a whole thing happening.

00:13:37.586 --> 00:13:41.255
I know. But my mom came by today
and apologized to me and my dad...

00:13:41.464 --> 00:13:44.132
...and it seems like she's changed.

00:13:46.967 --> 00:13:52.429
Hey, if my parents got back together,
and my dad found a job...

00:13:52.638 --> 00:13:56.765
...then my life could go
back to normal again.

00:13:57.140 --> 00:13:59.183
Maybe I should stay away
for a little while.

00:13:59.392 --> 00:14:02.060
First-date stuff: Candy, flowers.
It's easy.

00:14:02.269 --> 00:14:04.728
- Candy, flowers. Right.
- But it's times like these...

00:14:04.937 --> 00:14:08.564
...when a girl
needs her boyfriend the most.

00:14:09.607 --> 00:14:11.816
Boyfriend?

00:14:12.025 --> 00:14:15.777
Well, I mean, aren't we...?

00:14:17.236 --> 00:14:18.862
L... I guess.

00:14:19.029 --> 00:14:22.281
I've just never been a boyfriend before.

00:14:22.490 --> 00:14:25.241
- But you've had girlfriends?
- Yeah.

00:14:25.408 --> 00:14:29.953
No, not girlfriends,
just girls that, you know...

00:14:32.913 --> 00:14:35.706
Your mom. Saturday night.
Can't wait.

00:14:35.915 --> 00:14:37.290
Great.

00:14:40.834 --> 00:14:44.712
The fact is, yes, I admit it.
I occasionally talk about Summer.

00:14:44.920 --> 00:14:49.298
Maybe I even talk about her too much,
but that's not really the point, is it?

00:14:52.175 --> 00:14:53.426
Hi.

00:14:56.219 --> 00:14:57.595
So get this.

00:14:57.762 --> 00:15:02.306
Anna thinks all I ever do
is talk about Summer.

00:15:04.141 --> 00:15:06.225
I mean, that's crazy, right?

00:15:06.434 --> 00:15:08.727
You want me to lie?

00:15:10.520 --> 00:15:12.563
I'm that guy?

00:15:12.771 --> 00:15:16.106
Dude, how can I be that guy?
I hate that guy.

00:15:16.315 --> 00:15:18.691
No wonder Summer doesn't have
any interest in me...

00:15:18.900 --> 00:15:20.734
...because apparently all I do...

00:15:20.943 --> 00:15:24.195
...is I talk about Summer.
Although you'd think she'd like that.

00:15:24.403 --> 00:15:26.321
- You're doing it again.
- Right.

00:15:31.324 --> 00:15:33.701
I'm sorry I had to cancel
our date last night.

00:15:33.909 --> 00:15:36.828
- What time did you get home?
- Almost 2.

00:15:37.036 --> 00:15:41.497
- What was the last-minute crisis?
- You know I'm not at liberty to say.

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:46.792
Is Rachel's boyfriend
as understanding as I am?

00:15:47.001 --> 00:15:49.669
Rachel doesn't have a boyfriend.

00:15:49.878 --> 00:15:51.837
Go figure.

00:15:53.213 --> 00:15:57.299
Some people who don't like their life
make work their life.

00:15:58.675 --> 00:16:00.384
Well, that's not me.

00:16:00.551 --> 00:16:04.970
And I'll tell you this, if our settlement
conference goes well today...

00:16:05.179 --> 00:16:07.680
...I could be home by 6.

00:16:07.889 --> 00:16:10.891
Is that a bribe, counselor?

00:16:15.310 --> 00:16:17.103
Hey!

00:16:21.898 --> 00:16:26.567
- Did you have the talk?
- No. I like to lead by example.

00:16:29.027 --> 00:16:32.904
You and Julie Cooper trapped on a boat?
Can't wait to see how that one goes.

00:16:33.113 --> 00:16:37.240
I don't really have a choice,
since she's my girlfriend.

00:16:37.449 --> 00:16:39.950
What? Girlfriend?

00:16:40.159 --> 00:16:42.118
I thought that you didn't do girlfriends.

00:16:42.327 --> 00:16:44.245
Well, you did them, but you,
you know...

00:16:44.453 --> 00:16:48.122
I don't, and this is not a good way
to start. At least you'll be there.

00:16:48.331 --> 00:16:51.791
I won't. Who'd I bring?
I can't take Summer.

00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:55.585
Or I could...
Do you think she'd go? I don't know.

00:16:55.794 --> 00:16:58.003
I'm doing it again! Yeah!

00:16:58.212 --> 00:17:01.047
You know who you could ask?

00:17:02.965 --> 00:17:05.300
I could take a friend. Interesting.

00:17:08.010 --> 00:17:12.054
Okay, I'm never gonna mention
Summer's name to you again.

00:17:12.262 --> 00:17:17.391
Except for that. From now on, we'll only
discuss things we both have in common.

00:17:17.599 --> 00:17:20.226
Like how do you feel
about Newport charity events?

00:17:20.434 --> 00:17:21.852
- I hate them.
- Me too.

00:17:22.018 --> 00:17:24.145
So, what do you say you come
with me to one...

00:17:24.353 --> 00:17:26.271
...and we'll just quietly mock people?

00:17:30.357 --> 00:17:34.318
- Is Summer gonna be there?
- I don't know. Who cares?

00:17:37.070 --> 00:17:40.905
If anything happens between me
and Summer, you won't hear about it.

00:17:41.114 --> 00:17:43.407
I promise. On our friendship.

00:17:48.493 --> 00:17:50.453
Okay.

00:17:50.661 --> 00:17:54.247
The U.S. Fish and Wildlife Services'
ecological risk assessment asserts...

00:17:54.455 --> 00:17:58.249
...that the land adjacent to the wetlands
should be considered wetlands as well.

00:17:58.458 --> 00:18:00.584
Well, why stop there, counselor?

00:18:00.793 --> 00:18:04.086
Why not include the land adjacent
to the land adjacent to the wetlands?

00:18:04.295 --> 00:18:07.047
Mr. Nichol, I'm sure
your attorney has explained...

00:18:07.213 --> 00:18:10.465
...that soon the state will acquire
the land by eminent domain.

00:18:10.674 --> 00:18:13.592
It took the state five years
to purchase the Balboa Wetlands.

00:18:13.801 --> 00:18:15.594
Let's cut to the chase, shall we?

00:18:15.802 --> 00:18:20.388
How much is the Land Trust
offering me for Balboa Heights?

00:18:21.347 --> 00:18:23.223
Mr. Cohen.

00:18:23.432 --> 00:18:27.684
I was beginning to wonder
about your involvement in all of this.

00:18:30.645 --> 00:18:34.272
Thank you all for coming.
This meeting is adjourned.

00:18:34.480 --> 00:18:37.941
- Where are you going?
- Well, I mean, that's it?

00:18:38.149 --> 00:18:41.026
That's your whole dog-and-pony show?

00:18:41.235 --> 00:18:44.070
I'm disappointed.
What have you two been doing?

00:18:44.653 --> 00:18:48.156
Kiki tells me that you've been
in the office alone together every night...

00:18:48.364 --> 00:18:50.240
...till 2 in the morning.

00:18:51.616 --> 00:18:55.744
- Feel free to counter, Mr. Nichol.
- Why is she doing all the talking?

00:18:55.952 --> 00:18:59.746
Are you just here to ensure that your firm
makes the early edition again?

00:19:00.288 --> 00:19:03.540
"Father and son-in-law
fight for the Heights."

00:19:03.749 --> 00:19:07.293
Cal, I've dealt with a lot
of shady characters in my work...

00:19:07.501 --> 00:19:10.545
...but I've never seen anyone
stoop as low as you.

00:19:10.753 --> 00:19:13.963
You'll poison anything, air, water,
even your daughter's marriage...

00:19:14.172 --> 00:19:17.966
...as long as you profit.
- You've been living off my profits.

00:19:18.174 --> 00:19:21.301
If you think I'm bought and paid for...

00:19:24.553 --> 00:19:28.431
...just wait till I get you on the stand.
Don't let my silence here mislead you.

00:19:28.639 --> 00:19:31.391
I'm taking you down.

00:19:31.599 --> 00:19:33.142
Counselor.

00:19:40.438 --> 00:19:43.273
I think I hit a nerve.

00:19:57.782 --> 00:20:01.410
- I forgot I had this dress.
- Happens to me all the time.

00:20:01.618 --> 00:20:04.870
My mom bought it for me.
It seems appropriate.

00:20:05.079 --> 00:20:08.873
I think your mom would understand
if you didn't want to do this.

00:20:09.081 --> 00:20:11.249
Except I do.

00:20:11.458 --> 00:20:13.834
Right. That's what I meant.

00:20:14.960 --> 00:20:19.963
Marissa, this event is important
and on a yacht...

00:20:20.171 --> 00:20:23.674
...and whenever I go to these things,
somebody gets into a fight.

00:20:23.882 --> 00:20:25.967
You're gonna be fine.

00:20:29.427 --> 00:20:31.470
Ryan, hi.

00:20:31.679 --> 00:20:35.056
Oh, it's so nice to see you
in your room again.

00:20:35.264 --> 00:20:39.017
- You can sleep here tonight, if you want.
- It's okay.

00:20:39.225 --> 00:20:40.476
But thanks.

00:20:40.684 --> 00:20:43.061
Just thought I'd ask.

00:20:43.269 --> 00:20:45.229
Oh, I love this dress.

00:20:45.437 --> 00:20:48.272
Remember when we bought it,
we had lunch in Beverly Hills?

00:20:48.397 --> 00:20:51.691
- We saw Catherine Zeta-Jones.
- Yeah, I remember.

00:20:51.900 --> 00:20:53.484
So much fun.

00:20:55.027 --> 00:21:00.071
Well, we should get to the ship and
help out. Will you check on Kaitlin?

00:21:00.280 --> 00:21:02.156
Okay, sure.

00:21:04.532 --> 00:21:09.494
So I know that you and I
haven't always seen eye to eye...

00:21:10.578 --> 00:21:13.413
...but I want to say that I'm sorry.

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:16.874
You've been there for Marissa.
You care about her, I see that now.

00:21:17.082 --> 00:21:21.501
And I'm hoping that this party
will be a chance for us to start fresh.

00:21:21.710 --> 00:21:24.003
A celebration of a new beginning.

00:21:25.587 --> 00:21:27.589
I don't really like boats.

00:21:29.340 --> 00:21:31.216
Please?

00:21:34.301 --> 00:21:35.677
Okay.

00:21:36.302 --> 00:21:38.012
Thank you.

00:21:41.139 --> 00:21:42.765
Hey.

00:21:46.142 --> 00:21:48.727
Well, let's get to the boat, huh?

00:21:50.186 --> 00:21:51.812
Come on.

00:21:54.731 --> 00:21:58.358
I can't believe the lit mag won't publish
my limericks. That's censorship.

00:21:58.566 --> 00:21:59.859
It's censorship!

00:22:00.067 --> 00:22:04.528
- I'll organize a protest immediately.
- Fine, something involving a bra-burning.

00:22:04.737 --> 00:22:05.988
Cohen!

00:22:06.196 --> 00:22:08.698
- Hey. What are you still doing here?
- Detention.

00:22:08.906 --> 00:22:10.449
You live a hard life, Summer.

00:22:10.657 --> 00:22:14.368
A Paul Frank sale is more important
than the fall of the Ming Dynasty.

00:22:14.576 --> 00:22:17.161
What am I supposed to learn?
That opium is gnarly?

00:22:17.370 --> 00:22:20.830
Right.
Because there is no lesson there.

00:22:22.289 --> 00:22:24.708
Are you making fun of me? I can't tell.

00:22:24.916 --> 00:22:28.502
Most of the time, Summer,
you do my job for me.

00:22:28.710 --> 00:22:31.670
Again, not tracking.

00:22:33.713 --> 00:22:38.091
So, Cohen, I was wondering if you could
catch me up in history tomorrow.

00:22:38.299 --> 00:22:41.802
I can't until Sunday.
I have a charity thing tomorrow.

00:22:42.010 --> 00:22:44.470
- The thing for the children's hospital?
- Yeah.

00:22:44.678 --> 00:22:47.764
- You're going to that?
- We both are.

00:22:47.930 --> 00:22:50.307
- You and her?
- Me and Anna.

00:22:51.474 --> 00:22:53.726
Which is my name, by the way.

00:22:55.435 --> 00:22:56.894
I'm going too.

00:22:57.061 --> 00:22:59.479
Hey. Well, then I'll see you there.

00:23:00.647 --> 00:23:04.858
In fact, I'm going with him. Chip!

00:23:06.275 --> 00:23:08.527
- Hey.
- All right.

00:23:09.569 --> 00:23:11.570
She's going with him?

00:23:12.613 --> 00:23:14.155
I don't care.

00:23:23.870 --> 00:23:26.329
- There's pot roast in the...
- I ate.

00:23:26.538 --> 00:23:28.831
- With Rachel?
- What was that today?

00:23:29.039 --> 00:23:33.000
- I'm sorry. He just...
- lf you have a problem, come to me.

00:23:33.209 --> 00:23:37.795
You're never here. Who am I gonna
talk to if I don't talk to my dad? Seth?

00:23:38.003 --> 00:23:41.756
We're adults with demanding jobs.
You don't go running off to your daddy.

00:23:41.964 --> 00:23:45.133
If that's too hard, go give Jimmy a call.

00:23:45.341 --> 00:23:47.885
So nice talking to you.

00:23:54.305 --> 00:23:56.849
Don't ever get married.

00:23:58.016 --> 00:24:02.477
So how's everything going
with your relationship?

00:24:02.686 --> 00:24:04.687
Which I need to talk to you about.

00:24:04.895 --> 00:24:06.896
Good, I guess. Good.

00:24:07.105 --> 00:24:09.648
- It's just hard.
- Really?

00:24:09.857 --> 00:24:12.942
Seventeen years later,
it doesn't get any easier.

00:24:13.859 --> 00:24:15.819
It's her mom, really.

00:24:16.027 --> 00:24:18.154
In-laws.

00:24:18.362 --> 00:24:21.781
If you figure it out, let me know.

00:24:25.783 --> 00:24:27.701
- Good luck.
- Thank you.

00:24:30.745 --> 00:24:31.995
Thanks.

00:24:39.959 --> 00:24:41.793
Good evening.

00:24:50.632 --> 00:24:51.883
I'll call you.

00:25:05.975 --> 00:25:07.976
- Hey.
- Hi.

00:25:11.604 --> 00:25:14.856
Just got to get my good pair of shoes.

00:25:15.314 --> 00:25:18.316
I know this isn't exactly
the date you had planned...

00:25:18.483 --> 00:25:20.859
...but I really appreciate it.

00:25:21.068 --> 00:25:24.028
You couldn't have done better
with my mom yesterday.

00:25:24.236 --> 00:25:26.905
She's like a different person.

00:25:29.073 --> 00:25:33.492
Who knows? Maybe if everything
goes well tonight, then...

00:25:37.370 --> 00:25:39.955
I'm really happy.

00:25:40.163 --> 00:25:43.248
Which never used to be
an accomplishment.

00:25:44.416 --> 00:25:48.293
- And not just about my parents.
- We're gonna be late.

00:25:53.338 --> 00:25:55.298
- Yo.
- What up, homes?

00:25:55.506 --> 00:25:57.132
- Chilling.
- All right.

00:26:02.886 --> 00:26:05.429
- What's that smell?
- Perfume.

00:26:05.637 --> 00:26:08.389
It smells like wood chips.

00:26:08.556 --> 00:26:11.391
In a rose garden, roses.

00:26:11.558 --> 00:26:14.601
So this is your crib.

00:26:15.560 --> 00:26:17.395
This is where all the magic happens?

00:26:17.603 --> 00:26:20.939
If by "magic" you're referring to
the card game, then sadly, yes.

00:26:21.147 --> 00:26:23.607
You have a hot tub. Ever use it?

00:26:23.815 --> 00:26:27.151
Hot tub's for the ho's.
I usually hang in the grotto.

00:26:28.026 --> 00:26:29.944
- Hey, guys.
- Hi.

00:26:30.153 --> 00:26:33.280
- I'm just gonna run to the girls' room.
- I gotta go too.

00:26:33.488 --> 00:26:36.657
Right. Because girls can't be alone.

00:26:39.242 --> 00:26:42.994
What? It's Anna. I could've said "pop
a squat" in front of her if I wanted to.

00:26:43.203 --> 00:26:45.037
Sometimes you talk just to make sounds.

00:26:45.245 --> 00:26:47.038
Sometimes I do.

00:26:47.247 --> 00:26:48.873
So Anna looks good.

00:26:50.374 --> 00:26:53.209
Tonight should be fun.
There's gonna be a raffle.

00:26:53.376 --> 00:26:56.294
The only thing more fun
than a raffle is anything, really.

00:26:56.461 --> 00:26:59.004
- You guys ready?
- The girls are peeing.

00:26:59.213 --> 00:27:02.631
- Seth, don't say "pee."
- Where's Sandy?

00:27:02.840 --> 00:27:04.174
Don't ask.

00:27:05.550 --> 00:27:08.969
- Question.
- Hey. Early-bird special.

00:27:09.177 --> 00:27:12.638
I'm gonna soldier on. Trying to get
out of here at a decent hour.

00:27:12.846 --> 00:27:18.058
Right. Not all of us have
cocktail parties to go to on yachts.

00:27:21.518 --> 00:27:23.144
Right.

00:27:24.854 --> 00:27:28.898
So Caleb won't sell.
No surprise there. On to plan B.

00:27:29.106 --> 00:27:31.858
- What's plan B?
- I'm working on it.

00:27:32.025 --> 00:27:35.819
Come to the floor, Sandy. Everything
makes more sense on the floor.

00:27:36.027 --> 00:27:37.862
We've got pad thai on the floor.

00:27:38.070 --> 00:27:41.656
- We got work to do.
- Which is why we must refuel.

00:27:41.864 --> 00:27:43.865
You got any dumplings?

00:27:44.616 --> 00:27:46.659
I'm powerless before dumplings.

00:27:46.867 --> 00:27:48.994
Go with gravity, man.

00:28:06.838 --> 00:28:11.049
Thank you so much for coming.
Thank you. Nice to see you.

00:28:11.258 --> 00:28:13.009
- Hi, you're here!
- Hey, Mom.

00:28:13.509 --> 00:28:14.760
- How are you doing?
- Good.

00:28:14.968 --> 00:28:16.803
- Hi.
- Hi, Kaitlin.

00:28:17.011 --> 00:28:18.262
Hi, Ryan.

00:28:19.805 --> 00:28:23.599
Kaitlin doesn't trust new people,
but Ryan is very trustworthy.

00:28:24.683 --> 00:28:28.060
Marissa, Reverend Donahue
wants to say hello.

00:28:28.268 --> 00:28:29.561
Okay, Daddy.

00:28:31.145 --> 00:28:33.813
- Can I get a photo of the Cooper family?
- Totally, yes.

00:28:34.022 --> 00:28:36.773
- Come on, let's do it. Jules?
- Yes, of course.

00:28:36.982 --> 00:28:39.567
Riviera Magazine. It's very exciting.

00:28:39.775 --> 00:28:42.027
Ryan, why don't you join us?

00:28:42.235 --> 00:28:45.446
No. It's for your family.

00:28:45.654 --> 00:28:47.489
Say "cheese!"

00:28:49.073 --> 00:28:50.782
I didn't say "cheese."

00:28:50.949 --> 00:28:53.617
- Hey, Kiki.
- Hey, Dad.

00:28:54.868 --> 00:28:57.161
Where's the Sandman?

00:28:57.370 --> 00:29:01.747
- Those earrings are hypnotizing me.
- They're making me seasick.

00:29:02.957 --> 00:29:06.125
There he is, built like a pipe cleaner
but looking sharp.

00:29:06.334 --> 00:29:08.293
Same to you.
I don't know what that means.

00:29:08.460 --> 00:29:11.128
- Who's this little firecracker?
- It's my date.

00:29:11.337 --> 00:29:14.172
My friend Anna.

00:29:14.380 --> 00:29:17.215
- Clearly, she needs no introduction.
- Nice to meet you.

00:29:17.424 --> 00:29:21.343
Seth said you were scary,
but I see an inner sweetness.

00:29:21.551 --> 00:29:25.054
- I like your moxie.
- Suddenly we're in a film noir.

00:29:25.554 --> 00:29:29.348
The ocean is, like, so vast.
Like, endless.

00:29:29.556 --> 00:29:33.059
- I feel so...
- Insignificant?

00:29:33.267 --> 00:29:34.518
Go figure.

00:29:34.726 --> 00:29:37.103
You know, I'm thirsty.

00:29:37.311 --> 00:29:41.272
- Do you want to go to the bar?
- Yeah, you can. Thanks.

00:29:44.191 --> 00:29:46.609
You must have met Seth before.

00:29:56.865 --> 00:29:58.783
Excuse me.

00:30:00.576 --> 00:30:02.369
Hi, Ryan.

00:30:03.536 --> 00:30:06.288
- Good party.
- Thank you.

00:30:07.330 --> 00:30:09.665
And thanks for not telling Marissa.

00:30:09.873 --> 00:30:13.918
She's excited about you maybe
getting back together with her dad.

00:30:15.168 --> 00:30:18.837
You may be okay
with lying to Marissa, but not me.

00:30:19.046 --> 00:30:20.922
This is my life. My daughter.

00:30:21.130 --> 00:30:23.257
My girlfriend.

00:30:23.465 --> 00:30:28.885
Ryan, stay out of this.
It's none of your business.

00:30:39.850 --> 00:30:42.227
Hey, how goes it with Chip?

00:30:42.435 --> 00:30:46.396
He's surprised that the ocean is big.
Smoke another beer, Chip.

00:30:46.605 --> 00:30:48.564
Wow, someone's in a good mood.

00:30:48.773 --> 00:30:51.900
What is Seth Cohen doing
with Tinker Bell? She's from Pittsburgh.

00:30:52.108 --> 00:30:53.776
That's like the 909 of the East.

00:30:53.984 --> 00:30:56.402
- Anna's cool.
- She's a little scammer.

00:30:56.611 --> 00:30:59.529
First thing she does
is go after Caleb Nichol's grandson!

00:30:59.696 --> 00:31:01.531
Have you seen the way
she looks at him?

00:31:01.739 --> 00:31:06.325
- No, but clearly you have.
- Only because it's, like, totally obvious.

00:31:06.534 --> 00:31:08.910
Yes, it is, that you're jealous.

00:31:09.119 --> 00:31:11.370
- You like Seth Cohen.
- No!

00:31:11.579 --> 00:31:15.206
- You like him. Like him. Love him.
- Stop it!

00:31:15.414 --> 00:31:18.083
Stop! I do not like Seth Cohen.

00:31:18.291 --> 00:31:21.418
I can't like Seth Cohen.
He's, like, Seth Cohen.

00:31:21.627 --> 00:31:25.212
Well, it's too bad, because he likes you.

00:31:36.094 --> 00:31:37.553
Hey.

00:31:39.012 --> 00:31:41.973
My parents are totally getting along.

00:31:42.181 --> 00:31:45.391
If my dad finds a job soon,
I can be your neighbor again.

00:31:45.600 --> 00:31:48.977
- I could sneak over whenever.
- Parents are weird.

00:31:49.185 --> 00:31:51.479
I wouldn't count on anything.

00:31:51.687 --> 00:31:54.605
Right. You wouldn't.

00:31:56.231 --> 00:31:58.108
What's that mean?

00:31:58.316 --> 00:32:00.818
If you don't understand
how important this is...

00:32:01.026 --> 00:32:02.819
I get it.

00:32:03.027 --> 00:32:05.029
I get it, okay?

00:32:05.237 --> 00:32:07.363
Too well. My mom, my dad...

00:32:07.572 --> 00:32:11.074
Just because that happened to you,
doesn't mean it'll happen to me.

00:32:11.283 --> 00:32:14.368
- My parents may get back together.
- No.

00:32:15.077 --> 00:32:17.078
They won't.

00:32:17.286 --> 00:32:20.372
Why can't you just be happy for me?

00:32:21.497 --> 00:32:25.208
- Your mom is seeing Caleb Nichol.
- What? What are you talking about?

00:32:25.416 --> 00:32:28.960
I saw them together
in front of your house.

00:32:31.754 --> 00:32:33.296
I'm sorry.

00:32:44.553 --> 00:32:47.764
At this point, we go to the state
for Proposition 50 funds...

00:32:47.972 --> 00:32:51.057
...and hope they've got
a spare $200 million in the budget.

00:32:51.266 --> 00:32:54.518
Wait. I have the budget
here somewhere.

00:32:55.602 --> 00:32:58.937
It's with the Fish and Wildlife stuff.

00:32:59.146 --> 00:33:02.648
No, you put it
with the Land Trust documents.

00:33:03.982 --> 00:33:06.025
Feels like Twister.

00:33:06.234 --> 00:33:10.736
When I was in college,
that game got me in a lot of trouble.

00:33:10.945 --> 00:33:12.904
I can imagine.

00:33:13.697 --> 00:33:16.198
However, you and I
are in enough trouble as it is.

00:33:16.407 --> 00:33:17.782
Yeah.

00:33:17.991 --> 00:33:22.744
Was it me, or did your father-in-law
basically accuse us of having an affair?

00:33:23.828 --> 00:33:26.413
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:33:26.621 --> 00:33:29.081
Where'd he get that idea, right?

00:33:29.290 --> 00:33:35.585
I mean, we work together,
and we eat all our meals together.

00:33:37.712 --> 00:33:42.423
We talk on the phone
when we can't actually be together.

00:33:50.428 --> 00:33:53.555
I got a boat to catch.

00:34:16.527 --> 00:34:18.612
Oh, goodness.
Look at that piece right there.

00:34:18.821 --> 00:34:21.739
Get a northeasterly breeze,
that toupee's gonna go overboard.

00:34:21.906 --> 00:34:25.200
Good thing his wife has surgically
enhanced flotation devices.

00:34:25.408 --> 00:34:29.327
- Then she can jump in after it.
- Yeah, and they're also fun to look at.

00:34:29.536 --> 00:34:32.204
Do me a favor and go tell
that kid puberty started.

00:34:32.412 --> 00:34:35.414
I don't think the pencil-thin mustache
is gonna make a comeback.

00:34:35.623 --> 00:34:37.582
Hey, dude, embrace the razor.

00:34:37.791 --> 00:34:40.126
Sounds like you're speaking
from experience.

00:34:40.334 --> 00:34:43.961
Maybe when I was 13,
my nickname used to be Magnum, P.I.

00:34:44.170 --> 00:34:47.589
- Really?
- Yeah. Mothers can be so cruel.

00:34:50.590 --> 00:34:54.551
God, there are not people
like this in Pittsburgh.

00:34:54.760 --> 00:34:59.388
- You must hate Newport.
- I did. At first.

00:34:59.596 --> 00:35:03.098
But now it's growing on me.

00:35:09.144 --> 00:35:12.729
Are you thirsty at all?
I'm feeling a little parched.

00:35:12.938 --> 00:35:16.231
I think I'm gonna get a couple
of Mountain Dews to take the edge off.

00:35:16.440 --> 00:35:19.609
- Sure.
- Okay. I'll be right back.

00:35:22.694 --> 00:35:24.695
Wow. Check it out.

00:35:24.904 --> 00:35:28.197
It's, like, totally dark but totally visual.

00:35:28.406 --> 00:35:31.574
Yeah. Not understanding a word
you're saying.

00:35:31.783 --> 00:35:34.451
Finish 'shrooming.
I'm gonna go get a drink.

00:35:34.618 --> 00:35:38.871
Excuse me. I hate to interrupt.
Just a moment of your time.

00:35:40.163 --> 00:35:44.874
I'm Julie Cooper, the coordinator
of this event. Thank you all for coming.

00:35:45.083 --> 00:35:49.461
Through your generous contributions,
we've raised almost $200,000...

00:35:49.669 --> 00:35:52.046
...for the children's hospital.

00:35:52.921 --> 00:35:55.214
And don't forget, it's tax-deductible.

00:35:56.090 --> 00:35:59.008
- Can we talk?
- Yeah. Okay.

00:36:02.719 --> 00:36:05.346
I have to say that
we could not have done any of this...

00:36:05.554 --> 00:36:07.847
...without Caleb Nichol.
- Let's get out of here.

00:36:08.056 --> 00:36:10.182
I should leave and let her
get away with this?

00:36:10.390 --> 00:36:12.392
Let's give him a big hand.

00:36:12.600 --> 00:36:14.643
Is that what you would do?

00:36:15.644 --> 00:36:17.270
Hi.

00:36:25.983 --> 00:36:28.068
Oh, God! No.

00:36:29.569 --> 00:36:31.320
What's happening here?

00:36:33.571 --> 00:36:35.865
I like Seth Cohen.

00:36:36.073 --> 00:36:37.616
You...? You what now?

00:36:37.782 --> 00:36:39.575
Nothing. I wasn't talking to you.

00:36:39.784 --> 00:36:43.203
But if you tell anyone
what you heard here, I'll kill you.

00:36:47.497 --> 00:36:51.041
There's my beautiful daughter,
Marissa. Please join us.

00:36:54.334 --> 00:36:56.461
Come join us, honey.

00:37:00.547 --> 00:37:03.549
Thank you. Now my daughter
Kaitlin will pick the winner...

00:37:03.757 --> 00:37:06.050
...of the romantic getaway raffle.

00:37:06.259 --> 00:37:09.260
Marissa, would you like to
announce the lucky couple?

00:37:09.469 --> 00:37:11.012
Thanks.

00:37:11.220 --> 00:37:14.722
And how about another round
of applause for my mom?

00:37:16.723 --> 00:37:18.891
And for Caleb Nichol.

00:37:20.809 --> 00:37:23.728
After all their work
on behalf of the children's hospital...

00:37:23.895 --> 00:37:27.230
...if anybody deserves
a romantic getaway for two...

00:37:27.438 --> 00:37:30.149
...it's my mom and Caleb Nichol.

00:37:30.607 --> 00:37:34.735
I mean, aren't they
just the perfect couple?

00:37:34.901 --> 00:37:37.820
They've been keeping
their romance a secret...

00:37:38.028 --> 00:37:42.239
...but tonight, the secret's out.

00:37:44.824 --> 00:37:47.243
Congratulations, you guys.

00:38:04.837 --> 00:38:06.838
Honey, take this.

00:38:07.047 --> 00:38:10.924
- Don't start with me.
- After tonight, I'm done with you.

00:38:11.132 --> 00:38:14.218
- You're Caleb's problem now.
- Jimmy...

00:38:15.010 --> 00:38:16.719
One more, please.

00:38:16.928 --> 00:38:19.179
Excuse me.

00:38:19.388 --> 00:38:22.139
And the winner of tonight's raffle is...

00:38:22.348 --> 00:38:25.600
...Sandy and Kirsten Cohen.

00:38:30.853 --> 00:38:33.605
- What the hell was that?
- You lied to me.

00:38:33.772 --> 00:38:37.315
- You said you wanted us to be a family.
- I do.

00:38:37.524 --> 00:38:40.901
I was going to tell you,
but this is all so new.

00:38:41.110 --> 00:38:43.986
I know you've been through so much.
Marissa, honey...

00:38:44.195 --> 00:38:48.698
...this whole party was to show you
that our life could be like it was.

00:38:48.906 --> 00:38:51.366
You could move back home.
We could be a family again.

00:38:51.574 --> 00:38:54.284
And what about dad?

00:38:54.493 --> 00:38:59.329
Honey, I will always love your father.

00:39:00.622 --> 00:39:03.540
But because of what he's done,
we have no future together.

00:39:03.707 --> 00:39:05.625
Neither do we.

00:39:12.337 --> 00:39:14.672
Wait. Okay. What?

00:39:14.881 --> 00:39:17.466
Julie Cooper and my grandfather?

00:39:18.508 --> 00:39:22.802
If that worked out,
then Marissa would be my aunt.

00:39:22.969 --> 00:39:25.429
I can't believe
you missed all the excitement.

00:39:25.637 --> 00:39:27.805
Where have you been?

00:39:28.014 --> 00:39:32.141
I find raffles to be extremely upsetting.
There's too much suspense.

00:39:32.558 --> 00:39:34.268
I don't go.

00:39:43.982 --> 00:39:48.652
I trusted you. I told you things
about my life and my marriage.

00:39:48.860 --> 00:39:51.278
And you used them against me.

00:39:51.487 --> 00:39:54.405
And you tell me nothing about you.

00:39:56.323 --> 00:39:59.158
If this is the way you're gonna react...

00:39:59.325 --> 00:40:01.160
...do you blame me?

00:40:02.035 --> 00:40:03.286
No.

00:40:03.494 --> 00:40:06.371
In fact,
outside the office from now on...

00:40:06.580 --> 00:40:09.707
...we have nothing to say to each other.

00:40:10.957 --> 00:40:14.126
Oh, and good luck
with your new girlfriend.

00:40:14.334 --> 00:40:16.127
You're gonna need it.

00:40:16.336 --> 00:40:18.587
- I'm here.
- We're leaving.

00:40:18.796 --> 00:40:20.422
But I wore a jacket.

00:40:29.969 --> 00:40:32.804
I think this party's over.

00:40:34.722 --> 00:40:37.265
Want me to take you back to your dad's?

00:40:38.349 --> 00:40:41.435
I think I'm ready for our first date.

00:40:43.394 --> 00:40:46.938
I think we're way past that now.

00:40:48.689 --> 00:40:52.525
So in theory, Julie Cooper
could become your stepmother?

00:40:52.733 --> 00:40:54.526
Don't even say it.

00:40:54.735 --> 00:40:57.612
- I'm late to one event, I miss everything.
- Not everything.

00:40:57.778 --> 00:41:01.406
We won the raffle.
A romantic getaway for two.

00:41:01.614 --> 00:41:05.575
- Lf you can get away from the office.
- Yeah. It'll be good for us.

00:41:05.783 --> 00:41:09.577
- Spend a little time alone.
- Glad to hear it.

00:41:09.786 --> 00:41:11.745
So, what are you doing now?

00:41:14.956 --> 00:41:16.415
You.

00:41:18.041 --> 00:41:20.001
Glad to hear it.

00:41:45.600 --> 00:41:47.976
This is a pretty good date.

00:41:48.185 --> 00:41:51.729
- I just wish it didn't have to end.
- It doesn't.

00:41:51.937 --> 00:41:53.855
Spend the night.

00:41:56.773 --> 00:42:00.401
We don't have to do anything.
We could sleep.

00:42:01.610 --> 00:42:04.362
Really? Sandy and Kirsten
are cool with that?

00:42:04.570 --> 00:42:07.739
Well, I haven't had the talk yet, so...

00:42:10.407 --> 00:42:12.200
Do you snore?

00:42:12.408 --> 00:42:13.784
No.

00:42:13.951 --> 00:42:15.994
Well, I don't think so.

00:42:16.202 --> 00:42:19.246
I've never actually
slept with someone before.

00:42:19.454 --> 00:42:23.624
Me neither. I'm usually climbing out
the window or back into the front seat.

00:42:23.832 --> 00:42:27.209
- Okay, enough sharing.
- Yeah.

00:42:27.418 --> 00:42:29.044
Good night.

00:42:37.382 --> 00:42:39.925
I thought you said you wanted to sleep.

00:42:40.134 --> 00:42:42.719
Suddenly not so tired.

00:42:46.555 --> 00:42:47.805
Best...

00:42:49.431 --> 00:42:51.349
...date...

00:42:51.558 --> 00:42:53.392
...ever.
